From c0dda15b673d0fad3c69a855737bff7ad2ef27c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:43:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Remove a self join only when one of its subjects depends on
 the join references

A join of a logical source with itself on the same references was always
replaced by the parent subject of the same row. That is right only when all
the rows with the same join values give the same parent subject, or the same
child subject (with a constant predicate and no graph map); otherwise each
row is joined with every row with the same join values (RMLTC0033a,
kg-construct/rml-core). GTFS-Madrid-Bench, STOP_TIMES joined with itself on
trip_id: 2,364 triples instead of 43,008 at scale 1.

All the join conditions are now compared, not only the first one.
Test: rdfizer/tests/test_self_join.py.
